designCompareTools.description:
Compare the MOTION of a component from two frame sequences (reference vs candidate), each a directory of frames or an array of frame paths captured over time. Returns motion energy, temporal rhythm (signature correlation), motion_status (compared | static | capture_unreliable), and motion_score (number or null). Read motion_status before trusting motion_score: null means inconclusive, not a perfect 100. static and capture_unreliable never imply a score of 100. Includes a motion-signature chart when returnVisuals is true.

exec tool declaration:
```ts
declare const tools: { mcp__design_compare__compare_motion(args: {
  // Candidate frame sequence — a directory of frames or an array of paths.
  candidate: string | Array<string>;
  // Cap frames loaded per sequence (default 240).
  maxFrames?: number;
  // Reference frame sequence — a directory of frames or an array of paths (captured over time).
  reference: string | Array<string>;
  // Include the motion-signature chart (reference vs candidate over time).
  returnVisuals?: boolean;
}): Promise<CallToolResult>; };
```

